  "_comment": "Test start states, reachable by typing a short code in the Danger Zone. Read by scripts/game/StateCode.gd, which loads this file directly rather than through Content — nothing in the game proper reads it, and a debug affordance should not be merged into the runtime catalogue. Each preset is a patch applied over a fresh install, so a field left out means 'as a new save has it'. Codes use only glyphs that are unambiguous in the pixel font (see issue #60): the letters DFHJKMNPQTVWXY and the digits 23456, which leaves no vowels, so they are consonant skeletons rather than words. They are also a tappable list on the screen — typing one is the fallback, not the path. Every beat boundary in docs/FIRST-THIRTY.md is a state worth reaching directly, and beats 0 through 7 are the first five entries here.",
